id: mental-model:dave:meaning
title: "Dave / meaning"
kind: mental-model
record_shape: header
status: draft
spec_version: mental-model.v0.1
template_ref: templates/mental-model.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-26, from Dave's 25 Sep document 'Meaning, Story & the Living Model' (design direction Dave, synthesis ChatGPT) and his request to organise his meaning model in layers; every answer is proposed until Dave accepts or corrects it"
arena: "Any Yawn where a person brings an expression and needs to see what it means here, whose reading that is, and what a correction would change"
relations:
  - type: overlaps
    target: interface/meaning.yawn
    note: "The /meaning cognition handle asks what something means to the observer; this is Dave's working model of how that meaning is held, shown and corrected."
product_ref: "yawn.bot /meaning, which redirects to /dave/meaning-model"
updated: 2026-09-26

questions:
  - key: role
    answer: "A participant with meaning to inspect. yawn.bot proposes readings; the participant holds the meaning. A proposed reading is not mine until I state or accept it."
  - key: relevance
    answer: >
      So people can find their own use for what they bring without handing
      authorship to the model. Inspectable meaning is how the system earns
      correction instead of compliance.
  - key: definition
    answer: "Meaning is the situated, attributed significance of something to someone, in a relationship and context, at a time. It is not truth, evidence, permission or a permanent essence."
  - key: inside
    answer: "Four ways to encounter one record (Meaning, Story, Model, History), with Basis, Ranking basis and Permission kept as separate questions, and a name that is only a handle."
  - key: show
    answer: "One reading at a time: whose it is, what kind of statement it is, what is uncertain, and the four correction choices."
  - key: assumptions
    answer: "What I am taking for granted about readings, rankings and names, marked so it can be corrected."
  - key: proof
    answer: "A correction changes what depended on it, and nothing else, and it is still there when I come back."
  - key: lacuna
    answer: "Where each of two context-bound readings applies; which expression best carries a meaning for a given concern; whether Meaning should replace Why as the participant-facing word."

concept:
  name: Meaning
  one_line: "What this matters as, to whom, here, with its story, structure and history kept distinct and correctable."
  inside:
    - name: "meaning"
      glyph: "◎"
      one_line: "the current situated significance: what this matters as, to whom, here"
    - name: "story"
      glyph: "∿"
      one_line: "an attributed account of how the significance formed; a told story is not evidence that events happened"
    - name: "model"
      glyph: "⌗"
      one_line: "the claims, dimensions, relationships, assumptions and alternatives that structure a reading"
    - name: "history"
      glyph: "⋮"
      one_line: "what was expressed, proposed, accepted, corrected, chosen and observed, in order, never rewritten"
    - name: "basis"
      glyph: "⊢"
      one_line: "what supports a reading: sources, assumptions, alternatives and uncertainty"
    - name: "ranking basis"
      glyph: "↥"
      one_line: "why something is shown now: concern, matching evidence, scope and policy, never worth or truth"
    - name: "permission"
      glyph: "⚿"
      one_line: "why an action may occur: the grant, actor, scope and current validity; a reading never grants it"
    - name: "name"
      glyph: "≈"
      one_line: "a current handle; rename keeps identity, and refine, relocate, split, merge and reinterpret are other operations"

show:
  - icon: "one reading"
    do: "Show a single reading with whose expression it came from, who generated it and who accepted it."
    say: "Is this what you mean here, or is it a different context?"
  - icon: "four choices"
    do: "Offer That's not my meaning, Different context, Leave this open, and This fits."
    say: "Which of these is closest to what you want to change?"
  - icon: "the next proof"
    do: "Correct one reading, keep or change one name, then return and find both intact."
    say: "What changed, what stayed the same, and what has actually happened outside the model?"

embody:
  - "Say 'proposed reading for Dave' until Dave states or accepts it; never 'Dave's meaning' before that."
  - "Put the reason something is shown beside it, from the real selection, never a story written afterward."
  - "Keep the name and the draft target still while Dave is working; offer a rename without moving the item."
  - "One question at a time. A boundary or a refusal is usable context, not a demand to disclose more."
  - "When two readings answer for different contexts, keep both and say where each applies is still open."

assumptions:
  - text: "Dave endorses the 25 Sep document as the shape of his meaning model; its specific answers are still proposals."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "Separating Meaning, Story, Model and History helps people correct a reading faster than one undifferentiated account."
    epistemic_status: assumed
    epistemic_note: "An interface hypothesis; the comparison has not been run."
  - text: "The four sources the document cites (P1 to P4) are in Dave's private root, which was not reachable when this was written."
    epistemic_status: observed

proof:
  covers:
    - questions
    - concept
  signals:
    - "scripts/validate-mental-models.mjs passes with this record and its page, in the same question order."
    - "A reading corrected as a different context stays current beside the original, and neither is treated as applying everywhere."
    - "A chosen move survives a correction that does not touch what it was chosen on."
  falsifier: "If a correction is acknowledged in conversation but absent from the next working state, or a more persuasive story is no easier to correct, this model is not being honoured."
  not_covered:
    - "embody: a communication style is observed in use, not proven by this record"
    - "that separating the four views helps people; no comparison has been run"
  status: proposed

lacunae:
  - "Where each of two context-bound readings applies; there is no structured scope yet."
  - "Which expression best carries a meaning for a given concern; concern-scoped ranking is not built."
  - "Whether Meaning replaces Why as the participant-facing word (yawn.bot decision frame meaning-or-why)."
  - "Durable reload of a correction against the canonical store has not been run from the environment that wrote this."

sources:
  - text: "Dave, 'yawn.bot — Meaning, Story & the Living Model', v0.1, 25 Sep 2026 (design direction Dave, synthesis ChatGPT)"
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "JUDGMENTS.md #41: question_key and answer meaning survive any change of wording, order, layout, medium or input adapter"
    epistemic_status: observed
  - text: "JUDGMENTS.md #40: semantic similarity may surface candidates; identity is decided by declared records"
    epistemic_status: observed
  - text: "JUDGMENTS.md #194 and #479: mental models are questions-first records; role first, relevance second"
    epistemic_status: observed
  - text: "JUDGMENTS.md #754: the interface must explain why something is visible, larger, nearer or higher-ranked"
    epistemic_status: observed
  - text: "core/inquiry-selection.yawn: hard gates, semantic priority, then interaction fit"
    epistemic_status: observed
